1
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:31,900
Excuse me. My name is Richard Stewart.

2
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,252
I'm a photographer.

3
00:00:33,252 --> 00:00:34,700
May I take a picture of you and your little boy?

4
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:35,800
What's it for?

5
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:36,000
It's for a book.

6
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:36,800
Richard Stewart, 46 Linden Street,

7
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:37,700
You're writing a book?

8
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:38,900
It's a book of pictures.

9
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:40,900
I call it Family Album, U.S.A.

10
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,400
Oh, that's a nice idea.

11
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,700
Well, it's fine if you take our picture.

12
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:45,300
I'm Martha Vann.

13
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:48,068
Thank you. I appreciate your help.

14
00:00:48,068 --> 00:00:49,600
I'm Richard. What's your name?

15
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,000
Gerald.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:51,574
How old are you, Gerald?

17
00:00:51,574 --> 00:00:52,700
Five.

18
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,300
And where do you live?

19
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,758
We live in California.

20
00:00:54,758 --> 00:00:58,100
Well, welcome to New York.

21
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:01,013
OK, just a second.

22
00:01:01,013 --> 00:01:02,466
I'm almost ready here.

23
00:01:02,466 --> 00:01:03,649
Can I help you?

24
00:01:03,649 --> 00:01:10,575
Oh, please.

25
00:01:10,575 --> 00:01:16,500
Hold Gerald's hand, please. Great!

26
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:19,800
Now point to the buildings.

27
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:23,000
Terrific!

28
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:29,671
Give Mommy a kiss, Gerald. Nice!

29
00:01:29,671 --> 00:01:31,637
Thank you, Gerald.

30
00:01:31,637 --> 00:01:33,090
And thank you, Mrs. Vann.

31
00:01:33,090 --> 00:01:33,795
Oh, my pleasure.

32
00:01:33,795 --> 00:01:35,100
We'll be looking for your book.

33
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:40,800
Thank you. Good-bye. Bye, Gerald.

34
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:42,391
Thanks again.

35
00:01:42,391 --> 00:01:43,800
Oh, you're welcome.

36
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:45,100
Hey, let me take your picture!

37
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:52,500
Wonderful. Please.

38
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:53,848
Are you from New York?

39
00:01:53,848 --> 00:01:55,345
No, I'm from Greece.

40
00:01:55,345 --> 00:01:57,700
I'm an exchange student.

41
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:58,700
When did you come here?

42
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:00,100
Three months ago.

43
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:02,100
Your English is very good.

44
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,262
Thanks.

45
00:02:03,262 --> 00:02:08,900
I studied English in school.

46
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,013
Would you like some coffee?

47
00:02:10,013 --> 00:02:11,700
No, thank you.

48
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:13,600
Tell me about your book.

49
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,100
Oh, it's not finished yet,

50
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:16,600
but I have some of the pictures.

51
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:17,600
Would you like to see them?

52
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,400
Yes. I'd like that.

53
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:25,725
Here they are. Family Album, U.S.A.

54
00:02:25,725 --> 00:02:27,600
It's an album of pictures of the United States:

55
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:30,200
the cities, the special places, and the people.

56
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,300
And these are pictures of people working:

57
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:41,900
steelworkers, bankers, police, street vendors,

58
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:45,900
ambulance drivers, doctors....

59
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:50,300
Oh, this is my father. He's a doctor.

60
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:51,800
This is my mother.

61
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:52,000
What's her name?

62
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:55,096
Ellen.

63
00:02:55,096 --> 00:02:56,500
My younger brother, Robbie.

64
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,359
He goes to high school.

65
00:02:58,359 --> 00:03:00,200
This is my sister Susan.

66
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:03,200
She works for a toy company.

67
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:06,800
Here's my grandfather. He lives in Florida.

68
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,503
And this is my wife Marilyn.

69
00:03:08,503 --> 00:03:09,600
Oh, she's very pretty.

70
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:12,949
Thanks. And what about your family?

71
00:03:12,949 --> 00:03:15,000
They are in Thessaloniki.

72
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,200
That's a large city in northern Greece.

73
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,600
But now I'm living in the Bronx.

74
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,300
With a Greek-American family?

75
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:26,600
No. Hispanic.

76
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:29,500
Oh no! It's five thirty.

77
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:30,714
Will you excuse me?

78
00:03:30,714 --> 00:03:32,700
I have to meet my wife.

79
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:33,864
It was nice meeting you.

80
00:03:33,864 --> 00:03:35,000
It was a pleasure meeting you, too.

81
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,100
Thanks for your help.

82
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:39,000
And good luck! I've got to go.

83
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
By the way, I'm Richard.

84
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,100
What's your name?

85
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,000
Alexandra.

86
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:42,900
Bye-bye, Alexandra. Thanks.

87
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:45,900
Bye-bye. Richard! Richard! You left your bag!
